<spell-notebook "dropdown theming">
	<header level="1">
		Dropdown
		<header>A dropdown allows a user to select a value from a series of options.</>
	</>
	<dropdown-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<html>
			<ui-menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
				<ui-item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
				<ui-item link="#themes">Themes</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-dropdown-*` tokens: set one on the element or on any ancestor (`:root` included).
			They inherit into the shadow root, where the sheet reads each through a private alias, so nothing inside blocks
			them. Style the pieces with `::part()`: `trigger`, `text`, `icon`, `menu`, `item`, `label`, `search` and
			`clear`.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			ui-dropdown::part(menu) {
			  max-height: 20em;
			}
			ui-dropdown {
			  --ui-dropdown-arrow-size: 0.8em;
			}
			```
		</>
		<message state="info" size="small">
			<markdown>
				Variations build on the tokens: `floating` and `pointing` swap in their own `--ui-dropdown-floating-*` /
				`--ui-dropdown-pointing-*` values. A `button` dropdown reads the button tokens. Never set the
				`--_ui-dropdown-*` names: they're the sheet's private plumbing.
			</>
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-dropdown" playground>
				<ui-dropdown label="File">
					<ui-item>New</>
					<ui-item description="ctrl + o">Open...</>
					<ui-item description="ctrl + s">Save as...</>
					<ui-item kind="divider"></>
					<ui-item>Edit</>
					<ui-item>Share</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			The theme menu above picks the theme for every page of the site:  Spell, Glass, Fruity or Merlot,
			each restyling this component through its tokens.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
